-- title:
--   Local principal regular generator from invertibility after open immersion
-- statement:
--   Let $\varphi\colon X \to Y$ be a morphism of schemes which is an open immersion, let $J$ be quasi-coherent ideal sheaf data on $Y$, and let $x$ be a point of $X$. Assume that the pullback ideal sheaf data $J.\mathrm{comap}\,\varphi$ on $X$ is invertible in the sense of the project predicate `IsInvertible`: for every point of $X$ there are an affine open $W$ of $X$ and a section $f \in \Gamma(X, W)$ with that point in $X.\mathrm{basicOpen}\,f$, together with an element $g$ of the non-zero-divisors of $\Gamma(X, X.\mathrm{affineBasicOpen}\,f)$ such that the ideal of $J.\mathrm{comap}\,\varphi$ on the affine open $X.\mathrm{affineBasicOpen}\,f$ is the principal ideal $(g)$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an affine open $U$ of $Y$, a proof that $\varphi(x) \in U$, and a section $g \in \Gamma(Y, U)$ lying in the ideal $J.\mathrm{ideal}\,U$, such that, writing $\mathfrak p$ for the prime ideal of $\Gamma(Y, U)$ corresponding to the point $\varphi(x)$ of the affine open $U$ and passing to the localisation $\Gamma(Y, U)_{\mathfrak p}$, the ideal generated by the image of $J.\mathrm{ideal}\,U$ equals the span of the image of $g$, and the image of $g$ is a non-zero-divisor in $\Gamma(Y, U)_{\mathfrak p}$.
--
--   This is the pointwise local-generator form of invertibility for an ideal sheaf: at each point of the open subscheme where the pullback is invertible, the ideal becomes principal, with a regular generator, after localisation at the corresponding prime. It supplies the hypothesis shape needed for the effective Cartier divisor criterion, and is used in the construction of the schematic closure of an effective Cartier divisor on the generic fibre in the study of the modular curve $X_1(p)$.
